 } } \right| = 0$$


$$\therefore$$ $$\left| {\matrix{
   1 &amp; { - 1} &amp; { - 1}  \cr 
   1 &amp; 1 &amp; { - k}  \cr 
   k &amp; 2 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right| = 0$$


$$ \Rightarrow \left| {\matrix{
   0 &amp; 0 &amp; { - 1}  \cr 
   2 &amp; {1 + k} &amp; { - k}  \cr 
   {k + 2} &amp; 1 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right| = 0$$


${k^2} + 3k = 0 \Rightarrow k\left( {k + 3} \right) = 0$$


or $$k = 0$$ or $$-3$$

